\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Fixed-resource mean inference. The training boundary separates selection of a score control from the labels used for its held-out correction. Fold controls share one unlabeled sample; inference uses their weighted aggregate rather than independent copies of that sample. The returned asymptotic interval and its repeated-sampling assessment are distinct from an internal bounded construction that is not returned. No arrow denotes a validity certificate.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{Fixed-resource mean inference. The training boundary separates selection of a score control from the labels used for its held-out correction. Fold controls share one unlabeled sample; inference uses their weighted aggregate rather than independent copies of that sample. The returned asymptotic interval and its repeated-sampling assessment are distinct from an internal bounded construction that is not returned. No arrow denotes a validity certificate}{figure.caption.1}{}}
