\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Coverage and Monte Carlo uncertainty for all compared methods. Bars are the stored Clopper--Pearson intervals adjusted over all seven conditions and four methods; the dashed line is nominal coverage $0.95$. (a) Predictive conditions. (b) Information controls. Lower bounds for the frozen method remain below nominal throughout. In the rare-outcome condition, PPI++ has the lowest observed coverage, but its interval still contains nominal. These measurements are not finite-sample certificates.}}{8}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:coverage}{{3}{8}{Coverage and Monte Carlo uncertainty for all compared methods. Bars are the stored Clopper--Pearson intervals adjusted over all seven conditions and four methods; the dashed line is nominal coverage $0.95$. (a) Predictive conditions. (b) Information controls. Lower bounds for the frozen method remain below nominal throughout. In the rare-outcome condition, PPI++ has the lowest observed coverage, but its interval still contains nominal. These measurements are not finite-sample certificates}{figure.caption.7}{}}
